---
import AcademicLayout from "../../layouts/AcademicLayout.astro";
---

<AcademicLayout title="Governance & Ethics" currentSection="governance">
  <div class="container container-prose page-wrapper">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="badge-tier e0">ORGANIZATIONAL CHARTER</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Governance & Ethical Framework</h1>
      <p class="page-lead">
        Policies governing benchmark neutrality, conflict of interest management, privacy by construction, and zone interventions.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose-content">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Ethical Charter</h2>
        <p>
          Symnoesis is governed as an open, not-for-profit research initiative initiated by <strong>HarVa Groups</strong>. 
          Its core mission is to provide rigorous, unbiased, and reproducible measurement tools for human–AI interaction.
        </p>
        <p>
          The initiative adheres to five non-negotiable governance principles:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>No Pay-to-Rank:</strong> No system vendor can purchase evaluation placement, custom weighting, or expedited audit status.</li>
          <li><strong>Right of Reply:</strong> Any developer whose system is evaluated in the Symnoesis Index receives a 30-day pre-disclosure inspection window to verify reproducibility manifests.</li>
          <li><strong>Evidence Honesty:</strong> Synthetic sweeps (E1) are permanently demarcated from empirical trials (E2/E3). Numbers without audit trails are never published.</li>
          <li><strong>Open Science:</strong> Reference code is licensed under Apache-2.0; documentation and specifications are licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0).</li>
          <li><strong>Privacy Protection:</strong> Telemetry collection from private citizens is prohibited by architecture.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Conflict of Interest (COI) Policy</h2>
        <p>
          To maintain scientific neutrality:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>All maintainers and audit reviewers must publicly declare commercial affiliations, equity holdings, and consulting contracts.</li>
          <li>Reviewers with material ties to a participating AI vendor are recused from verifying or scoring that vendor's system.</li>
          <li>Funding sources are published transparently in <code>ORG_FACTS.yaml</code>.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Zone Intervention Protocols (Z1–Z7)</h2>
        <p>
          The specification pairs each governance zone with concrete operational recommendations:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Zone 1 (Mutualistic):</strong> Maintain standard monitoring. Support continuous human learning checkpoints.</li>
          <li><strong>Zone 4 (Watch):</strong> Trigger proactive inspection. Recommend user unaided practice intervals to halt skill atrophy.</li>
          <li><strong>Zone 5 (Dependence):</strong> Prompt system developers to review automated default boundaries. Require explicit confirmation for high-stakes steps.</li>
          <li><strong>Zone 7 (Critical Intervention):</strong> Halt public deployment or trigger emergency human oversight due to safety gate breach.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</AcademicLayout>

<style>
  .page-wrapper {
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: var(--text-h1);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 1rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .page-lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .prose-content {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .prose-content h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .prose-content p {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .prose-content ul, .prose-content ol {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prose-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
